#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:178
msgid "Prefix-Stable Packing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:180
msgid ""
"Prefix-stable packing is used for signatures that connect programmable "
"shader stages or carry patch constant data. Elements are visited in "
"declaration order and placed at the first compatible location in the 32-row "
"by 4-column register space. Once an element is placed it is never moved, so "
"appending elements to a signature does not change the locations assigned to "
"its existing prefix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:186
msgid ""
"Elements can share unused components in a row when all applicable packing "
"constraints are satisfied:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:189
msgid "Every element in a row must have a compatible interpolation mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:190
msgid ""
"When native 16-bit types are enabled, every element in a row must have the "
"same component width. Without native 16-bit types, min-precision values "
"occupy 32-bit components."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:193
msgid ""
"Within each row, elements are ordered by category: arbitrary values first, "
"followed by system values, and then system-generated values. For example, a "
"system value can never be packed to the left of an arbitrary value. "
"`ClipCull` and `TessFactor` follow these categories in the internal "
"ordering, with the additional placement rules described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:198
msgid ""
"A system value or system generated value cannot be placed in a dynamically "
"indexed row. A dynamically indexed row is a row within the range covered by "
"a multi-row element, where the row is selected using a dynamic index."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:202
msgid "Some semantic interpretations require additional handling:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:204
msgid ""
"`SV_ClipDistance` and `SV_CullDistance` are packed only with each other in "
"dedicated rows. Together they may occupy at most eight components across at "
"most two rows. The rows must be adjacent when a clip or cull element spans "
"multiple rows. Otherwise, clip and cull rows do not need to be adjacent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:208
msgid ""
"A multi-row tessellation factor is searched for only in the last column. "
"Arbitrary values may fill the columns to its left, even when declared after "
"the factor. A single-row tessellation factor is ordered and packed as a "
"system value instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:212
msgid "Geometry shader output streams are packed independently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:225
msgid ""
"Assuming `B` has column-major matrix orientation, the signature is allocated "
"as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:235
msgid "Indexed Packing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/SemanticSignatures.md:237
msgid ""
"Indexed packing is used for a pixel shader output signature. Each eligible "
"`SV_Target` element occupies one row and starts at column zero. Its semantic "
"index directly selects that row, so declaration order does not affect "
"placement and rows without a corresponding semantic index remain unused. "
"Elements that do not contribute to the target register space remain "
"unallocated."
msgstr ""
